{
  "$schema": "../../scenarios.schema.json",
  "version": "2.0.0",
  "notes": "Built-in tool journeys against a real KAS answered by the fake KRS: approve/deny gates, auto-trusted reads and searches, write and edit diffs, non-zero exits, and a multi-tool chain. Each scenario carries the turns that answer its prompts.",
  "scenarios": [
    {
      "id": "tool-shell-approve",
      "name": "Approve a shell command and see it run",
      "category": "tool-use",
      "description": "Agent proposes a shell command, the approval gate appears, the user approves once, the command executes, and the agent's synthesis lands in the transcript \u2014 the everyday approve-and-run tool workflow",
      "docRef": "/docs/cli/chat/permissions",
      "priority": "p0",
      "steps": [
        "prompt:print the tools sentinel",
        "waitForText:requires approval",
        "enter",
        "waitForIdle",
        "frame:after-approve"
      ],
      "verify": [
        "screen.contains:KIRO-TOOLS-OK-7391",
        "screen.contains:The shell command ran successfully",
        "screen.notContains:requires approval",
        "screen.notContains:Prompt already in progress",
        "screen.notContains:Standing by"
      ],
      "observe": "The shell tool surfaces an approval gate; approving once runs the command, and the agent synthesizes a final answer. Execution is proven by the synthesis reply, which is scripted on a turn that only fires once a tool result returns. The KIRO-TOOLS-OK-7391 assertion is NOT output-discriminating: on the success path the shell card collapses to a single line showing only the command, so the sentinel matches the echoed command text rather than stdout, which never reaches the frame. Asserting stdout would need the error path, where the card auto-expands and the result payload renders -- see the non-zero-exit journey, which asserts an exit code the command text cannot supply.",
      "engine": [
        "kas"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "scenario",
        "journey"
      ],
      "turns": [
        {
          "name": "ask-shell",
          "match": {
            "userInputContains": "print the tools sentinel"
          },
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "toolUse",
                "toolUseId": "tu-1",
                "name": "execute_bash",
                "input": "{\"command\":\"echo KIRO-TOOLS-OK-7391\"}",
                "stop": true
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "TOOL_USE"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "synthesize-after-shell",
          "match": {
            "hasToolResults": true
          },
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "content": "The shell command ran successfully."
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "END_TURN"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "background-catch-all",
          "times": 0,
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "content": "Standing by."
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "END_TURN"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tool-shell-deny",
      "name": "Deny a shell command and the agent adapts",
      "category": "tool-use",
      "description": "Agent proposes a shell command, the approval gate appears, the user denies it, the tool reaches a terminal Rejected state without executing, and the agent acknowledges and adapts \u2014 the deny-and-recover permission workflow",
      "docRef": "/docs/cli/chat/permissions",
      "priority": "p0",
      "steps": [
        "prompt:attempt the blocked command",
        "waitForText:requires approval",
        "arrowDown",
        "arrowDown",
        "enter",
        "waitForIdle",
        "frame:after-deny"
      ],
      "verify": [
        "screen.contains:Rejected",
        "screen.contains:Understood, I did not run that command",
        "screen.notContains:requires approval",
        "screen.notContains:Prompt already in progress",
        "screen.notContains:Standing by"
      ],
      "observe": "The shell tool surfaces an approval gate; denying it drives the tool to a terminal Rejected state without running, and the agent acknowledges and continues.",
      "engine": [
        "kas"
      ],
      "tags": [
        "scenario",
        "journey"
      ],
      "turns": [
        {
          "name": "ask-shell",
          "match": {
            "userInputContains": "attempt the blocked command"
          },
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "toolUse",
                "toolUseId": "tu-1",
                "name": "execute_bash",
                "input": "{\"command\":\"echo should-not-run\"}",
                "stop": true
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "TOOL_USE"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "synthesize-after-deny",
          "match": {
            "hasToolResults": true
          },
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "content": "Understood, I did not run that command."
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "END_TURN"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "background-catch-all",
          "times": 0,
          "respond": {
            "events": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "content": "Standing by."
              },
              {
                "type": "metadata",
                "stopReason": "END_TURN"
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
